1
00:00:00,590 --> 00:00:11,110
If this administration and any of the previous administrations truly cared about the so-called migration crises, they would stop causing it.

2
00:00:11,110 --> 00:00:17,170
It would stop intervening politically, economically, and militarily in the affairs of other nations.

3
00:00:17,490 --> 00:00:25,770
But it won't, because waging war at home and abroad is more profitable for the billionaires signing their checks.

4
00:00:26,550 --> 00:00:30,910
War in any of its forms has never been for the benefit of the people.

5
00:00:30,910 --> 00:00:42,110
And as the Trump administration wages war against the people of the United States, making billions for private companies, it is also waging war against the people of the world.

6
00:00:42,590 --> 00:00:46,850
Last week, it declared Cuba a national threat.

7
00:00:47,310 --> 00:00:52,130
Let's be clear. Cuba poses no threat to the United States.

8
00:00:52,130 --> 00:01:00,410
But for 67 years, the U.S. has strangled the Cuban economy, stealing nearly $15 million a day from the Cuban people.

9
00:01:00,870 --> 00:01:03,010
And now it tightens its news.

10
00:01:03,750 --> 00:01:06,090
Let's explore the level of hypocrisy.

11
00:01:06,210 --> 00:01:08,530
Our communities are being militarized.

12
00:01:09,090 --> 00:01:19,270
Civilians are being kidnapped without due process, taken from their jobs, from their homes, from their cars, and forced into concentration camps.

13
00:01:19,270 --> 00:01:23,070
Over 30 people have died in ICE custody this year alone.

14
00:01:23,230 --> 00:01:28,270
Children as young as two are being held in deplorable conditions.

15
00:01:28,750 --> 00:01:30,930
At least eight people have been shot and killed.

16
00:01:31,330 --> 00:01:35,550
We see the videos and we hear them lie to justify their crimes.

17
00:01:35,550 --> 00:01:48,870
We live in a country where brutal force normalizes racism, hatred for immigrants, for trans people, for women, where dissent is met with violence, where journalists are arrested for telling the truth.

18
00:01:49,030 --> 00:01:50,130
And this is not new.

19
00:01:50,510 --> 00:01:52,930
It's accelerating and it's intensifying.

20
00:01:52,930 --> 00:02:06,150
So we must ask ourselves, what authority does this morally bankrupt government have to impose its will on any other nation to violate the sovereignty and self-determination of people from other countries?

21
00:02:06,570 --> 00:02:06,950
None.

22
00:02:07,390 --> 00:02:10,250
They have no moral or legal authority.

23
00:02:11,070 --> 00:02:13,430
You can be sure they're not about democracy.

24
00:02:14,010 --> 00:02:15,330
They're not about freedom.

25
00:02:15,890 --> 00:02:17,070
Their God is profit.

26
00:02:17,070 --> 00:02:25,670
The only authority they claim is violence, is occupation, is extraction, the enslavement of other countries and their people.

27
00:02:26,230 --> 00:02:29,210
And with this, they produce mass migration.

28
00:02:29,990 --> 00:02:30,890
This is the legacy.

29
00:02:31,910 --> 00:02:32,570
Think slavery.

30
00:02:33,030 --> 00:02:33,710
Think Jim Crow.

31
00:02:34,050 --> 00:02:34,790
Mass incarceration.

32
00:02:35,470 --> 00:02:36,210
Think ICE.

33
00:02:36,750 --> 00:02:41,690
Think of how we, the people of this country, are denied the most basic things.

34
00:02:41,690 --> 00:02:47,130
Health care, education, how they create scapegoats but never solve the problem.

35
00:02:47,450 --> 00:02:53,130
How they force working people into debt for survival on stagnant, unlivable wages.

36
00:02:53,990 --> 00:02:59,530
For 67 years, the U.S. has punished Cuba for choosing to be free from its intervention.

37
00:03:00,290 --> 00:03:03,450
The world has denounced this for over 30 years.

38
00:03:04,010 --> 00:03:11,670
Cuba should not be punished for choosing not to be part of and complicit with the atrocities that we know the U.S.

39
00:03:11,690 --> 00:03:15,450
government administrations have been capable of.

40
00:03:16,070 --> 00:03:19,330
We don't need to agree in order to respect.

41
00:03:19,330 --> 00:03:25,230
But the United States government does not abide by that simple ethical standard.

42
00:03:26,070 --> 00:03:30,050
And now they label Cuba a national threat.

43
00:03:30,270 --> 00:03:30,590
Why?

44
00:03:30,970 --> 00:03:33,650
Because Cuba, again, chose freedom and dignity.

45
00:03:33,750 --> 00:03:37,050
Because Cuba chose doctors over bombs.

46
00:03:37,390 --> 00:03:41,530
Because Cuba's existence proves another way is possible.

47
00:03:41,690 --> 00:03:43,810
And that is the greatest threat of all.

48
00:03:44,070 --> 00:03:47,950
Proving that it is possible to be free from imperialism.

49
00:03:48,690 --> 00:03:49,970
I am not Cuban.

50
00:03:50,590 --> 00:03:51,830
Because I know you're going to come for me.

51
00:03:51,830 --> 00:03:57,870
And I don't need to be in order to know what the U.S. has in store for the Cuban people if they get their way.

52
00:03:57,870 --> 00:04:03,370
I was born in the most exploited congressional district in this country, the South Bronx.

53
00:04:03,870 --> 00:04:08,430
I am a working class black Caribbean woman, a daughter of immigrants.

54
00:04:08,830 --> 00:04:12,830
And that is why I have the right and I have the responsibility to say this.

55
00:04:13,290 --> 00:04:16,150
They are using our resources, our taxes.

56
00:04:16,550 --> 00:04:16,790
Yes.

57
00:04:16,790 --> 00:04:23,170
And our silence to launch wars on Cuba, Venezuela, Palestine, and so many other countries.

58
00:04:23,170 --> 00:04:25,470
We don't need trillions for war.

59
00:04:25,890 --> 00:04:27,130
We need dignified wages.

60
00:04:27,590 --> 00:04:28,530
We need health care.

61
00:04:28,650 --> 00:04:29,350
We need housing.

62
00:04:29,470 --> 00:04:30,210
We need education.

63
00:04:30,810 --> 00:04:32,590
We need ICE abolished.

64
00:04:32,590 --> 00:04:39,710
And we demand that the U.S. government gets its hands off Cuba, gets its hands off Latin America and the Caribbean.

65
00:04:40,230 --> 00:04:42,750
Let them develop within their right to sovereignty.

66
00:04:43,370 --> 00:04:47,670
Our struggle is one struggle and our enemy is the same.

67
00:04:47,990 --> 00:04:53,270
So U.S. hands of Cuba, hands of the world, people of the world, unite.

